            "review_title": "Review at Pho Cao Van",
            "review_text": "BL_Leo\nPetaling Jaya, Malaysia4019 contributions\n0\nGood ol bowl of beef pho\nApr 2020 • Family\nVietnam mini series - since it's MCO period, might as well speed up my post-Vietnam trip's food adventure to make way for the upcoming local ones soon. FYI.. I am not traveling at this moment (still under MCO). \n\nI remember our family trip to Vietname vividly. It was 15th December 2018 - and when our plane touched down at HCM airport at night, we were faced with transportation problem.. Vietnam had just beaten Malaysia in Suzuki Cup final and it sent the whole country into frenzy. Some opportunist public transport tried to charge us ridiculous amount but we didn't budge. We only manage to secure another van to send us to our hotel downtown about 2 hours later and we were so tired that we slept right away. \n\nThe very next morning, we woke up early and took taxi to our first breakfast spot - Pho Cao Van. Our itinerary in HCM City was planned by my bro-in-law who came to this city for working trip. It was a small shop that serves pretty good traditional beef pho - bear in mind that they do not speak English but good thing is that the choice is either beef or chicken, small or big. Just point at what you want to eat and then make small or big gesture.. lol! \n\nSoup is pretty tasty with generous amount of meat. As per Vietnamese standard, you can add as much bean sprouts, basil leaves and chilly as you prefer. We didn't stay too long because it could get pretty hot & stuffy after a while.\nRead more\nWritten April 8, 2020",
