            "review_text": "LamN\nSingapore, Singapore4905 contributions\n1\nCows come to Cao Van by van\nJan 2019 • Family\nWe came here based on some blog reviews - reportedly one of the few very good phở places in Sài Gòn that don’t run out of food by late morning. It’s not bad, but the broth is disappointing - not fragrant nor very flavourful. In fact, the broth at a few phở eateries in Paris or California is better! They are quite generous with the meat (which is tender and good), and you can even order extras (brisket, rare, crunchy meat balls, tendon). However, they don’t have a few delicious varieties, like tripes or cartilage. Service is very friendly. Hygiene is not of the highest standards, but you won’t get sick here. Very cheap: you can have your bowl of phở, a bowl of extra meat, a fresh juice and a towel for less than USD 5.\nRead more\nWritten January 17, 2019",
