            "review_title": "Review at Pho Cao Van",
            "review_text": "turine\nEdinburgh, United Kingdom42 contributions\n0\nOne of the most authentic pho in town\nFeb 2018 • Solo\nThe place has a long history for serving only 'Pho' as their specialty. As a true local who was born and grew up here, I can testify for their pho. Very hearty, Saigonese style of beef noodle. Don't compare to the Northern style of pho because they are different. Good local atmosphere that has a nostalgic look that dates back to pre-1975 Saigon. Highly recommended if you're looking for a truly local, old school southern pho experience. Bare in mind pho can be enjoyed anytime of the day. They close early though, like 9-10 pm.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 4, 2018",
